  "caption": "Every afternoon at 3pm, Quinn's head started to throb, starting at the back and creeping up behind the eyes. Quinn's theory: brain too big. Coffee didn't help.\n\nSome headaches start in the neck. Irritated upper-neck structures can refer pain into the head, which is known as a cervicogenic headache.\n\nWhat can help: hands-on care combined with deep neck flexor and shoulder-blade exercises, breaking up long postures, reviewing your pillow and sleep setup, and expecting gradual change over weeks rather than overnight.\n\nGet it checked promptly if you have a sudden severe headache, fever with a stiff neck, a recent head knock, numbness or other neurological changes, or a new headache pattern after 50.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
